Establishment of the Gender Mainstreaming Working Group in the Region

#### Article 8

1. In an effort to accelerate the institutionalization of Gender Mainstreaming in all Regional Apparatus Organizations, a Gender Mainstreaming working group in the Region shall be established.  
2. Members of the Gender Mainstreaming working group are all heads/leaders of Regional Apparatus Organizations.  
3. The Regent shall appoint the Head of Bappeda as Chair of the Regional Gender Mainstreaming Working Group and the Head of the Regional Apparatus Organization responsible for Women's Empowerment as Head of the Secretariat of the Regional Gender Mainstreaming Working Group.  
4. The establishment of the Regional Gender Mainstreaming working group shall be determined by Regent's Decree.

#### Article 9

The Regional Gender Mainstreaming Working Group as referred to in Article 5 paragraph (1) letter c has the following duties:

a. promoting and facilitating Gender Mainstreaming to each Regional Apparatus Organization;  
b. conducting socialization and advocacy of Gender Mainstreaming to the Sub-district Head (Camat) and Wali Nagari;  
c. preparing work programs every year;  
d. encouraging the realization of Gender Responsive planning and budgeting;  
e. preparing the work plan of the Gender Mainstreaming working group every year;  
f. being accountable to the Regent through the Vice Regent;  
g. formulating policy recommendations on gender mainstreaming to the Regent;  
h. preparing the Regional Gender Profile;  
i. monitoring the implementation of Gender Mainstreaming in each Regional Apparatus Organization;  
j. establishing a technical team to conduct analysis of the Regional budget;  
k. preparing a regional action plan on Gender Mainstreaming in the Region; and  
l. encouraging the implementation of selection and appointment of focal points in each Regional Apparatus Organization.

